---
epr-meta-version: 1
id: claude-hooks-governance
covers: subtree
---

`.claude/hooks/` — the thin hook-transport layer: PreToolUse gates (epr-meta compose-gate,
managed-surface discipline, sensitive-file/seed/cargo guards) and PostToolUse signal
accumulators (drift counters, sentinels). This manifest CLAIMS full responsibility for the
subtree (`covers: subtree`): the coverage walk terminates here.

**Considered, no enforcing rule yet (the deliberate opt-in, not a nag).** The real gates on
this tree are structural, and none is expressible as an enforced `.epr-meta` predicate:
(1) a hook file is INERT until registered in `.claude/settings.json` — an unregistered hook
is dead code, and registration is the review surface; (2) hooks are fail-open by contract
(any internal error exits 0 silently) with per-entry `timeout` in SECONDS (normalized
2026-07-02 — values had been written as milliseconds, making the declared 2-15s budgets
33min-4h no-ops); (3) hooks stay THIN — real logic lives in `.claude/scripts/_lib/` (tested
under `_lib/__tests__/`) or `.claude/scripts/memory-kit/` (tested under its `__tests__/`),
so the transport can be swapped (the brit/eprfs direction) without losing the rules. Add a
rule here only if a NEW recurring, mechanizable drift appears in this tree.
